From: Maharaja Kennadyrajan <quic_mkenna@quicinc.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Oct 2024 17:47:57 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] wifi-scripts: sbin/wifi: Add support to add MLO links

Add a new wifi command to add MLO links dynamically.

Usage:
wifi mlo_add_link <phy> <band> <interface-name> <vap-mac-addr>

Example:
wifi mlo_add_link phy00 2g wlan1 00:03:7f:12:12:61

Note:
interface-name is present in the /etc/config/wireless file.

Limitation with 6G link addition:
1. User can't add 6G link with this command when only one 6G vap
is brought up via wireless file.
2. User can add 6G link with this command when atleast two or more
6G vaps are brought up via wireless file.
3. Alder + WKK combination RDPs are not supported yet.

